From dd731b1295c1cfc29e1e19a2c40b2de87bdf06ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 00:47:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] GUI: build with Qt 4.8 again (guarded), for old macOS
 (10.5+, PowerPC)

Qt 5-only calls are wrapped in QT_VERSION checks or replaced by equivalents that exist in all
versions:
- QKeySequenceEdit (5.2): minimal QLineEdit-based stand-in for Qt < 5.2
- QRegularExpression: QRegExp under Qt 4
- QComboBox::setCurrentText: setEditText() / findText()+setCurrentIndex()
- QCompleter::setFilterMode, QLineEdit::setClearButtonEnabled (5.2): skipped under Qt 4
- QMenu::addSection (5.1): separator + disabled entry under Qt 4
- QHeaderView::setSectionResizeMode: setResizeMode() under Qt 4
- QTimer::singleShot with functor (5.4): slot-based deferral in RclMain
- qAsConst: std::as_const; QStringList::join(QChar): join(QString)
- QComboBox currentTextChanged/textActivated signals: Qt 4 equivalents
- <QStyleHints> include guarded

recoll.pro.in: on Qt 4 use QT += gui, pass -std=gnu++17 -Wno-register explicitly (no c++17
CONFIG feature, and qatomic_powerpc.h uses the register keyword), build the .qm files with an
extra compiler (no lrelease feature), skip SingleApplication, use the Qt 4 webkit module name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Voh3NXqrzFgK56iCnHqxZ2
